; Chance/timing notes draw on this disassembly; not playthrough-verified.

[Solution:overview:Overview]

Rescue princess Mara from Zarn's dungeon and bring her back to the
Great Valley.

Primary walkthrough: Jacob Gunness via the Classic Adventures Solution
Archive (file id 285), with August 2010 bug fixes by Jim Grimwood.
Dorothy Millard's Spectrum walkthrough (Tipshop / her homepage) is a
useful cross-check for optional farm food/coin and HELP/KISS variants
at the nymph.

#LIST
{ Random attackers may appear - KILL them WITH BOW (or WITH SWORD later) }
{ Save often; combat can miss }
LIST#

[Solution:notes-fatal:Fatal Moves]

#TABLE(default,centre)
{ =h Action | =h Risk }
{ SWIM | Drowning }
{ JUMP the chasm | Fall }
{ Climb the volcano wall without the rope | Fall }
{ ENTER HOVEL without wearing the ring | Witch }
{ Linger with spider / slime / demons / Zarn | Timed death after a few turns }
{ Meet the wolves without bow and arrows | Instant death }
TABLE#

[Solution:notes-random:Random Encounters]

Gunness: characters appear at random and may kill you - KILL creature
WITH BOW, and save often. Enemies listed in the route may also show in
adjacent locations.

Code inspection of the random helper: elf and flying lizard scenic
hits commonly use a 1/15 fatal roll per appearance; Korl warrior 1/20;
many bow attacks miss on a 1/5 roll and must be retried. Not
playthrough-verified.

[Solution:notes-timed:Timed Threats]

Spider, slime monster, demons and Zarn arm a short countdown on entry
(six turns in this binary). Clear them before it expires: KILL SPIDER
WITH BOW, KILL MONSTER WITH BOW, KILL DEMONS WITH SWORD, KILL
WIZARD/ZARN WITH SWORD. After the wolves injure you, wait/LOOK until
the wood nymph heals you before moving on.

[Solution:notes-optional:Optional Items And Variants]

Gunness skips farmhouse food and the woodman's coin. Millard collects
both; they are optional on this route. YS tips say kiss the nymph;
Gunness uses LOOK until healed, moves south, then GET RING. TOUCH ROCK
and RUB ROCK are treated as equivalent in tips. Tipshop's older Gunness
mirror inserts an extra S, W before the return BLOW HORN; the CASA file
(with Grimwood fixes) does not - this page follows CASA.

